# Razzle-Dazzler: 1/2; "Whenever you cast your second spell each turn, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. It can't be blocked
# this turn." Turn 1: Bot1 casts Mox Ruby, Mox Sapphire, then the Dazzler itself as the third spell (spells cast before it came in count,
# so no trigger: it was the third, not the second). Turn 2: Bot2's own second spell (Mox Ruby after an Ornithopter) does nothing.
# Turn 3: Bot1's second spell (Ornithopter, after Mox Pearl) triggers it: a counter (2/3) and no blocks this turn - Bot2's
# Ornithopter cannot block it, and 2 damage lands; the third spell adds nothing. Turn 5: only a first spell, so no counter and
# the Ornithopter blocks it again (the unblockable effect ended with turn 3).

